From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kp-cvd-adb <kp@cuttlefish>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlefish: initialize ProxyPair state members

[KBOX_VSOCK] Fix uninitialized members in ProxyPair
(common/libs/utils/socket2socket_proxy.cpp). The default constructor only
initialized stop_fd_, leaving `started_`, `c2t_running_` and `t2c_running_`
indeterminate, while the move constructor reads `other.started_` and
Start()/Running() read the same state.

On the normal accept path, `watched.push_back(ProxyPair())` move-constructs a
freshly default-constructed temporary. With a reused stack slot that still
holds a stale pointer (e.g. left by the previous loop iteration's
watched.remove_if() bookkeeping), `started_` can be read as a non-zero byte and
the FATAL "ProxyPair cannot be moved after Start() being executed" aborts
socket_vsock_proxy via SIGABRT, even though Start() was never called. This
surfaces as repeated proxy crashes and failed ADB readiness checks under
run_cvd/KASandbox.

Value-initialize started_ and both atomics, matching the upstream Android 16
code. This removes the undefined behavior at its source; it is not covered by
the FATAL check, which is intentionally kept.

---
diff --git a/common/libs/utils/socket2socket_proxy.cpp b/common/libs/utils/socket2socket_proxy.cpp
index 63cc631ca..dfe7371d1 100644
--- a/common/libs/utils/socket2socket_proxy.cpp
+++ b/common/libs/utils/socket2socket_proxy.cpp
@@ -101,10 +101,17 @@ class ProxyPair {
     LOG(DEBUG) << label << ": Proxy thread completed";
   }
 
-  bool started_;
+  // [KBOX] These members must be explicitly initialized: the default
+  // constructor does not set them, yet the move constructor reads `started_`
+  // (and Start()/Running() read the atomics) before any assignment. Relying on
+  // zero-initialized storage is undefined behavior; with a reused stack slot
+  // the move constructor can observe a garbage non-zero `started_` and abort
+  // with "ProxyPair cannot be moved after Start() being executed", crashing
+  // socket_vsock_proxy. Matches the upstream fix in Android 16.
+  bool started_ = false;
   SharedFD stop_fd_;
-  std::atomic<bool> c2t_running_;
-  std::atomic<bool> t2c_running_;
+  std::atomic<bool> c2t_running_ = false;
+  std::atomic<bool> t2c_running_ = false;
   std::thread c2t_;
   std::thread t2c_;
 };

2.34.1
